From b92a46436f1510e61a649c98f65b40f04810bde5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:58:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(input): read unaccelerated gesture deltas when
 wlroots carries them
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Swipe travel grows with finger speed because libinput's accelerated gesture
deltas are the only pair wlroots exposes (wlr_pointer_swipe_update_event
carries no unaccelerated fields). Consume the unaccelerated pair at a single
delta-selection point — niri parity: niri downcasts to libinput for the same
feed — behind UMBRIEL_WLR_GESTURE_UNACCEL, detected with cpp.has_member so
stock 0.20.x compiles the accelerated fallback unchanged. Client-forwarded
swipes stay on the accelerated pair.

swipe-test update takes an optional [unaccel_dx unaccel_dy] pair (defaults to
the accelerated pair, existing callers bit-identical) and reports
unaccel_support, so tests/harness/checks/input/swipe_unaccel.sh pins the
pipeline's delta source: travel follows the unaccelerated pair on a build that
carries it, the accelerated pair otherwise.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
